CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ names a later throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ names a later non-throwing member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The noexcept expression of a member declaration that cannot be evaluated
at the declaration (b is not yet declared) is kept for
implicit_exception_specifications.  The inner noexcept operator took its
failing operand to be true, so nothing was kept; and the retry had no
`this', so `b()' did not call S::b.  Now a specifier whose noexcept
operators had such an operand is kept, and the retry binds `this'
([expr.prim.this]/4).
